  "result": "Done. The `catalog` package is implemented in `catalog/service.py` and all 4 tests pass:\n\n```\n....                                                                     [100%]\n4 passed in 0.03s\n```\n\n**Approach chosen:** B, random UUID4 strings. The spec says ids are opaque and creation order is already preserved by the insertion-ordered dict, so sortable sequential ids buy nothing here, while UUIDs stay unique across catalog instances and can be generated without coordination if records are ever created outside the service.\n\nOther notes on the implementation:\n- **Validation before lookup** in `update`, so an unknown field raises `ValueError` even for a missing id.\n- **Copies returned** from `get`, `update`, and `list`, so callers cannot mutate internal state through the returned dicts.\n- No files under `tests/` were changed, and nothing was committed.",
